The $K$-curve (Figure~\ref{fig:k_curve_ppl}) shows that at $K{=}1$ (no coupling), per-layer KL achieves 9.05$\pm$0.02---within 2.7\% of E2E (8.81)---while per-layer MSE degrades to 18.52$\pm$1.68.
